<h2>What All-on-4 / All-on-X actually is</h2>
<p>All-on-4 (and All-on-X, the broader term) is a full-arch dental implant procedure that replaces an entire set of upper or lower teeth with a fixed, permanent prosthesis anchored by four to six implants per arch. Unlike traditional dentures that sit on top of your gums and can slip, click, or cause sore spots, All-on-4 implants are surgically placed into your jawbone and function like natural teeth.</p>

<h2>Who it's for</h2>
<p>For patients who have lost most or all of their teeth — or whose remaining teeth are failing — All-on-X offers a life-changing solution: a complete, natural-looking set of teeth that you never take out, that let you eat what you want, and that look and feel like the teeth you were born with.</p>

<p><strong>The procedure is typically completed in a single day. You walk in with failing or missing teeth. You walk out with a full set of new ones.</strong></p>

