<h2>The process, step by step</h2>
<ol class="checklist" style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:28px">
  <li><strong>Free consultation &amp; 3D scan.</strong> A comprehensive exam plus a CBCT (3D) scan. Dr. Phillips evaluates your case and gives you a clear treatment plan with transparent pricing &mdash; no pressure, no sales team.</li>
  <li><strong>Digital planning.</strong> Using your scan and digital impressions, a computer-guided surgical plan is created for millimeter-accurate implant placement.</li>
  <li><strong>Surgery day.</strong> Under sedation, failing teeth are removed, implants are placed, and a fixed set of temporary teeth is attached &mdash; all in one visit.</li>
  <li><strong>Final restoration.</strong> After about 3–6 months of healing, your final custom prosthesis is fitted &mdash; designed to look natural and built to last.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Recovery: what to expect</h2>
<p>Most patients are surprised by how manageable recovery is. Here's the honest timeline:</p>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>First few days.</strong> Some swelling and soreness are normal and usually controlled with over-the-counter medication or a short prescription. Most people take it easy for a day or two and return to desk work within a few days.</li>
  <li><strong>First few weeks.</strong> You'll wear your fixed temporary teeth and follow a soft-food diet while the implants integrate with your bone. You're eating and smiling the whole time — never without teeth.</li>
  <li><strong>3–6 months.</strong> Your bone fuses to the implants. Once healing is complete, we fit your final prosthesis and you can return to a normal diet.</li>
  <li><strong>Follow-ups.</strong> We see you at planned checkpoints to confirm healing, adjust the bite, and answer questions. Long term, you'll clean around the arch daily and come in for regular hygiene visits.</li>
</ul>

